## The lodge's claims: one of each kind the runner can settle, each under the
## rooms, things and verbs it needs. The shared set is the winning line. The
## hand bell is in it on purpose and bears on nothing.

claims
  needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Vault
  needs things: the valve, the hand bell, the strongbox, the deed
  needs verbs: turn, open, take

  claim the story can be won
    the story ends in victory

  claim the deed is in hand
    the player has the deed

  claim the warden has been asked about the vault
    the warden was asked about "the vault"
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall
    needs things: the warden
    needs verbs: ask

  claim the ledger has been studied
    the ledger is studied
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Study
    needs things: the brandy, the warden, the ledger
    needs verbs: take, give, read

  never the strongbox leaves the Vault
    the strongbox is not in the Vault
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Vault
    needs things: the valve, the strongbox
    needs verbs: turn, take

  claim the Study is reached
    the player is in the Study
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Study
    needs things: the brandy, the warden
    needs verbs: take, give

  never the Study is reached without the brandy
    the player is in the Study
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Study
    needs things: the hand bell, the warden
    needs verbs: take, give

  claim the notice has been read
    the notice is read
    needs rooms: the Porch
    needs things: the notice
    needs verbs: read

  claim the valve has been turned
    the valve has been turned
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry
    needs things: the valve
    needs verbs: turn

  claim the strongbox is open
    the strongbox is open
    needs rooms: the Porch, the Hall, the Pantry, the Vault
    needs things: the valve, the strongbox
    needs verbs: turn, open
end claims
